\section{Trace the Commitment, Then Enumerate Its Alternatives}

\begin{verbatim}
choose A by largest footprint
remove B and C from consideration     # Overlap is ownership.
fill uncovered operations with P,Q   # A exports their input u.

x = 0xA6 -> u = 0x4D
left:  v = 0x0D, w = 0x0E, y = 0x0F
right: p = 0x13, q = 0x1C
baseline: U,V,W,Y,P,Q          cost 15
greedy:   A,P,Q                cost  9
          # C also owns u, so A blocks it.
compare:  C,B                  cost  6
          # C must issue first because B reads its u.
\end{verbatim}

An exact reference can branch on the three ways to produce $y$: $A$, $B$, or singleton $Y$. If it chooses $A$, then $P,Q$ are forced, so the minimum in that branch is nine. If it chooses $B$, the cheapest way to supply $u$ and $q$ is $C$ at cost four; the singletons for $u,p,q$ would cost nine. That branch reaches six. With singleton $Y$, neither $A$ nor $B$ can be used, so $V$ and $W$ are required. They cost four on top of the two for $Y$, even before supplying the right arm, which costs at least four more. This exhausts the candidates and certifies six as the optimum. The identical hexadecimal results establish what each plan must compute at the test input; the ownership and operand checks establish why the two chosen instructions can be composed at all inputs.

\section{Use Search Where Commitments Matter}

Blindell distinguishes greedy techniques from exhaustive methods that prune combinations rather than commit immediately. A useful compromise is to run the greedy selector first, keep its verified cover as an upper bound, and search only a budgeted set of competing matches. A sound lower bound for each unfinished branch tells the selector when that branch cannot beat the incumbent; a ranking score need not have this property. In the example, reserving $A$'s singletons merely because their remaining cost looks small says nothing about branches that never selected $A$. Even a two-choice lookahead should check availability of all external operands and retain a legal fallback. If the time budget expires, reporting the best known legal solution is useful, but it does not certify a negative answer to a tighter decision budget. For example, cost nine says nothing about feasibility at budget seven; cost six is an explicit witness.
